            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0478" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/1764¾</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">20 May, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: As I intimated in the
                    little scribbled note I sent back by the special messenger whom you sent with
                    this to New York, I think your position in the conversation with the Austrian
                    Ambassador was admirable. We clearly cannot afford to consult with Germany as to
                    our course toward Great Britain. The two must be kept carefully separate and
                    distinct.</p>
                <p>I am glad to be back and at my desk.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
